## Experiments (hypotrack)

Experiments in this repository are tracked with `hypx` (see `.claude/skills/hypotrack/SKILL.md`). Three rules:

1. Before starting experiment work, read `hypx context --hyp <H..>`.
2. After looking at results, write your reading down with `hypx note <exp-id>`.
3. Record hypothesis verdicts with `hypx hyp conclude <H..> --status ... --evidence <exp-ids>`. Body: one verdict sentence, blank line, bulleted evidence.

Never submit an experiment without `hypx exp new` first; an experiment without a recorded intent must not exist.
